llenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=12611" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">blindjustice</a>. And especially to Debbie The <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/11_F.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/11_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/11_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=122678" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Barroness</a> for your celebratory comment and I agree, study of the times indeed.</td>', 'This challenge meant a lot to me because it aligns closely with the kind of photography I love, aside from portraiture. I’m drawn to street photography and what I''d like to call "fleeting (in)significance" that captures human-ness, frailty, and the raw truths of reality the ugly, the sad, and the honest. The things that often live far from the spotlight, but still deserve to be seen, understood, and even celebrated.

